        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43580235?u=cae42d5a371dd041072ce6d85a1808de05535be8&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a page for the CSS <code class=\"notranslate\">ruby-overhang</code> property.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>I've commented out the interactive example, it's not working for some reason.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>TODO:</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Fix / remove interactive example</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Update mdn/data</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">We're missing a docs page for it.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I took a look through relnotes from Jen Simmons' for Safari 18.2 which has some good examples:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>18.2 relnotes <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/16301/webkit-features-in-safari-18-2/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/blog/16301/webkit-features-in-safari-18-2/</a></li>\n<li>demo <a href=\"https://codepen.io/jensimmons/pen/azoOgbq?editors=1100\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://codepen.io/jensimmons/pen/azoOgbq?editors=1100</a></li>\n</ul>",
