        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF141 adds support for <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLDialogElement/closedBy\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLDialogElement.closedBy</code></a> and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/dialog#closedby\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">closedby</code> attribute on <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;dialog&gt;</code></a> by default in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1964078\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1964078</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note and removes the experimental feature note.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3166062421\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40028\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40028/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40028\">#40028</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40036",
            "title": "FF141 Relnote/Expr Feat closedBy/closedby on dialogs",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-24T12:45:19.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-23T04:10:37.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF141 adds support for <a href=\"http://localhost:5042/en-US/docs/Web/API/PointerEvent/persistentDeviceId\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">PointerEvent.persistentDeviceId</code></a> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1968400\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1968400</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release not and does minor formatting changes to the property page</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3166056814\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40022\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40022/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40022\">#40022</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40035",
            "title": "FF141 PointerEvent.persistentDeviceId - Relnote/layout",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-24T12:45:18.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-23T03:54:23.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112726619?u=6d16930d0e2054b2b458c320f6f8b85b602b8da2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The paragraph that aimed to be fixed contained 2 issues:</p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Logical error: there is no 'success'/'error' events on  DOM event type property, according to official specification <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#events-2\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#events-2</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The explanation text was just hard to read and focus, so it is a bit simplified and more concised</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I made this change, so the developers do not be confused with unexpected 'error' / 'success' DOM event types</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#events-2\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#events-2</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40025",
            "title": "Fixing explanations of onsuccess/onerror listeners for IndexedDB",
